## Scope

Follow [zotero/zotero#6055](https://github.com/zotero/zotero/pull/6055)
after submission by ticket 0787. Read the PR page for maintainer response and
CI, make requested changes on the fork branch, and record the upstream outcome.
`SYNC.md` owns the live status; this ticket owns the work and its evidence.

## Remaining verification from 0787

- Run the added `zoteroPaneTest.js` case in a built Zotero; only syntax was
  checked before filing.
- On a focused window, use real Tab and Shift+Tab keypresses to show the
  plugin-contributed button is reached, then update
  `plugins/sdt-sitter/RELEASE-NOTES.md` from that observation.

## Review findings already on the PR page

Every review on zotero/zotero#6055 was posted by the author's own GitHub
account — internal reviews and Claude Opus reviews — and each is recorded as
COMMENTED, not as an upstream verdict. No maintainer response, formal approval,
CI check or merge is recorded on the page. `SYNC.md` says the same.

The second review (submitted at `785e363`) reads, verbatim: "**Verdict:
BLOCKED** (changes requested, not a rejection). Nothing here crashes or is dead
code, but two design points about focus order and two gaps in the test are worth
settling before this lands." Its four itemized findings, headings as written:

1. "The opt-in marker contradicts the surrounding markup, and is undocumented"
   — "A plugin author who copies the adjacent built-in markup writes
   `tabindex="-1"` and is silently excluded — the failure is invisible, with no
   warning and no fallback." Asked for either documenting the attribute as the
   registration API or keying on something that does not collide with the house
   convention.
2. "Arrow navigation now jumps across the quick-search field" — "pressing → on
   "New Note" teleports focus over the search box and the pane toggle to the
   far-right plugin button, and ← comes back the same way. That is a
   discontiguous roving group".
3. "The test has a surviving mutant" — the `ArrowPrevious` fallback leg "is
   never asserted"; "Replace that fallback with `|| null` and the suite stays
   green." Also untested: the `disabled` and `display: none` legs of the
   `pluginButtons()` filter.
4. "The one Shift+Tab assertion cannot distinguish success from fallback" — the
   assertion "is almost certainly passing on the *fallback* branch", and
   "Accepting both outcomes makes the assertion insensitive to which one
   occurred."

Later reviews on the same page, same account, move past it: a re-review at
`f55d038` (BLOCKED, on the hidden/disabled/display-none cases being asserted but
not covered) and one at `a1d3eea` (APPROVED). The findings above are carried so
they survive the PR page, not as the page's current disposition.

## Exit criteria

The PR has an upstream disposition, requested revisions are resolved, and the
focused-window reading is recorded. If merged, confirm the route in an
upstream build before closing.
